---
title: Lamb Doner
servings: 2
course: Main
prep time: 20m
cook time: 10m
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
---

= Lamb Doner =

Preheat the oven to 220°C.

Place all of the doner ingredients (@lamb mince 20% fat{175%g}, @lamb leg meat{175%g}(fat removed), @garlic{2%cloves}(finely grated), @sea salt{0.5%tsp}, @bicarbonate of soda{0.5%tsp}, @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @ground paprika{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @dried chilli flakes{pinch}, and @black pepper{}(freshly ground)) into a #food processor{} and pulse until smooth. Divide the mixture in half. Shape each portion into a ball and roll out between two large sheets of baking paper, until very thin. Remove the top sheet of baking paper from each piece of meat. Bake for 3 to ~{4%minutes} until browned.

Remove the trays from the oven and carefully use a #blowtorch over the surface of the lamb until blackened in small areas. Leave to rest for a couple of minutes.

= Yoghurt Sauce =

Mix together the @plain yoghurt 0% fat{100%ml}, @mint leaves{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), @sugar{pinch}, and @salt{pinch}, and set aside.

= Serve =

Warm the @corn tortillas{2} on the top shelf of the oven for ~{1%minute} and place between two warmed plates.

Slice the lamb into strips, about 2.5cm wide. Serve the lamb on the open tortillas and top with the serving ingredients (@cabbage{40%g}(shredded), @cucumber{50%g}(thinly sliced), @tomatoes{2}(thinly sliced), @red onion{0.5}(thinly sliced), and @pickled chillies{6}), yoghurt sauce and @hot sauce{}, if using. Fill generously until unable to wrap.